WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:01.510
What was that?

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:02.810
It came from the mountain.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.070
It's a Cerulean!

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:15.950
Take this!

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.840
Are you all right?

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:38.420
You saved us!

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:39.430
Thank you so much.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:40.370
Who are you?

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:43.480
I'm Golden Snub-nosed Monkey,
a Cerulean Hunter.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:47.000
You really shouldn't go after Ceruleans 
that are bigger than yourself.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:49.900
Order: Primates
Family: Cercopithecidae
Genus: Rhinopithecus

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.900
Leave those to us Hunters. 
You could get eaten.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.870
It got the jump on us.

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:54.630
But, wow! You're not a Hunter for nothing!

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:57.520
It might still be here. Stay hidden, okay?

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:01.380
Kaban, may we go survey the situation?

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:03.000
Huh? Okay.

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:08.270
Did Boss just speak?

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:10.850
Oh, right. He doesn't normally, does he?

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:12.840
We're totally used to it by now.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:15.420
If you're going, we'll go with you.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:19.140
I think that Cerulean was 
the only one that got away.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.970
Still, when you're done with 
your business, please hide.

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:30.150
Come to think of it, what happens 
if a Cerulean eats you?

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:34.380
To say you'd die might be an exaggeration...

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:38.750
You can't talk anymore. 
And you'd forget about us, too.

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:39.700
Really?

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:43.510
I wonder why the Ceruleans 
come after us, anyway.

00:01:43.510 --> 00:01:46.490
Some say that they're eating Sandstar.

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:47.410
Huh?

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:51.580
Whatever the reason, it's like a forest fire... 
The best thing to do is run.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:55.800
What's this?

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:58.800
This is awful. What happened here?

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:04.520
That's the footprint of a Cerulean.
One that we're hunting.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:12.940
P-Please don't eat m—

00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:15.860
Who're these two?

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:18.250
I squashed the one that ran off 
in the opposite direction.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:23.280
Order: Carnivora
Family: Ursidae
Genus: Ursus

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:19.960
I defeated mine, too.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:23.280
Hard to believe the fragments that flew 
off of it can move, too. It's a strong one.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.520
What? That was only a fragment?

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:30.430
We've taken down an even bigger one before.

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:32.860
You mean the one we fought in the desert?

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:35.250
That could've been the end for the whole park.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:36.280
Where's the main body?

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:38.130
African Wild Dog is tracking it.

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:41.120
Well, the big ones are slow, anyway.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:41.930
Let's move.

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:44.250
Will you be okay? Isn't it dangerous?

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:46.760
If there's anything we can do to help...

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:52.450
Sandstar?

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:55.040
It's been erupting frequently 
since yesterday.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:57.530
Little ones happen all the time.
Come on, let's catch up.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:00.400
Warning. Warning.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:01.690
Announcement.

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:04.870
Sandstar Raw concentration is high.

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:07.600
Large-scale eruption may be imminent.

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:09.570
Warning. Warning.

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:12.040
They say Boss can actually talk.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:13.780
But what's he saying?

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:15.920
"Sandstar Raw"?

00:03:16.690 --> 00:03:20.220
Anyway, we're going to go 
take care of that Cerulean.

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:22.310
Huh? That's worrisome, too!

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:24.010
We can help!

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:27.630
You? You couldn't even handle 
that fragment earlier.

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:29.130
You'll only get in the way.

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:32.230
Or do the two of you want to try me?

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:36.000
Sorry.

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:42.390
I'd like to check the mountain. 
You two should wait here.

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:43.200
Huh?

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:48.940
Boss is acting funny. 
What should we do, Kaban-chan?

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:52.010
Let's check out the mountain.

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:52.710
Okay!

00:03:57.290 --> 00:04:01.550
Mirai-san said there was 
something on the mountain.

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:04.670
That Cerulean came from the 
direction of the mountain.

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:07.180
The footprints go that way, too!

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:10.930
Huh? Are they getting smaller?

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:11.960
That's weird.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:13.870
Wait, does that mean...

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:19.600
You could have let them down a little 
more gently, don't you think?

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:23.480
Weaklings like them just get in the way.

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:28.440
That's what you say, but you 
did it out of worry, didn't you?

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:31.730
We're catching up.

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:36.040
Am I imagining it, or are 
the footprints getting bigger?

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:41.080
Finally! This is too much 
responsibility for me.

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:44.880
Order: Carnivora
Family: Canidae
Genus: Lycaon

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:42.910
Your orders are rough.

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:44.030
Good work.

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:44.900
How's it look?

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:48.590
Like we thought, its size makes it slower.

00:04:48.590 --> 00:04:52.680
If it can't replenish its Sandstar fast enough, 
it might perish on its own.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:55.340
It really is big...

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:58.940
Do we have to fight it?

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:03.610
Remember, sometimes they change shape. 
We'll take it out now to be safe.

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:05.770
Use Wild Release from the start.

00:05:05.770 --> 00:05:08.370
Don't be stingy! Chip away at 
it to get to the stone first!

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:08.850
Right.

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:10.160
Roger that.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:15.260
The brown bear is the largest land animal 
in Japan. They love sweet things.

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:40.130
Tobu Zoo, Itakura-oniisan (Saitama)

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:20.170
They're timid and very cautious, 
and not the insatiable type.

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:25.890
They aren't friendly with humans so much 
as we have a convenient relationship.

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:30.180
On the other hand, they're curious animals 
and will lumber up to new things

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:34.290
to poke and prod them, and when 
they do that, it startles people.

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:36.790
Then the moment you move, 
that startles the bears in turn.

00:05:36.790 --> 00:05:39.050
That's a pattern that leads to bear attacks.

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:45.050
In English, <i>Lycaon pictus</i> is called the 
African hunting dog or the wild hunting dog.

00:05:40.790 --> 00:06:09.950
Yokohama Zoorasia, Tajima-oniisan (Kanagawa)

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:48.770
They have long, slender legs, 
incredible stamina, and big ears,

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:50.740
making their bodies adapted to hunting.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:54.360
What makes them different from other 
carnivores is how they can sprint more than

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:56.230
just a short distance before 
running out of breath.

00:05:56.230 --> 00:06:00.210
They catch their prey by taking turns 
as a pack to chase their prey

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:03.030
until it's too tired to get away.

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:05.800
They'll continue the chase 
over a distance of kilometers,

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:10.220
so this makes them an especially skilled 
hunting dog among African carnivores.

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:17.480
We've walked pretty far. 
Can we take a break?

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:20.190
Yeah. Sorry, Serval-chan.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:24.230
You're worried about everyone, huh, Kaban-chan?

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:25.220
Yeah...

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:30.430
Ceruleans are always really scary, but there's 
something different about this one.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:34.740
Here comes another message from Mirai-san.

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:40.170
We were right. That giant Cerulean was 
getting energy from the mountain somehow.

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:43.360
Because the black Cerulean has that ability,

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:47.840
we needed to re-affix the mountain's 
filter before attacking.

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:51.510
We were able to line up 
the four gods without issue,

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:53.540
and now we're about to descend the mountain.

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:56.870
We have to eliminate it 
by any means possible.

00:06:56.870 --> 00:06:59.640
Even if we've already evacuated 
all of the Friends to safety,

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:01.440
we can't leave that monster on this island.

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:08.990
It finally revealed its stone... 
Time to finish it off in one charge!

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:11.110
Roger that.

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:16.590
I'll put together a report later, 
but for now, we know that

00:07:16.590 --> 00:07:20.680
no matter how much you attack, the Cerulean 
keeps absorbing Sandstar Raw from the mountain,

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:23.600
it's heading in the direction of the sun,

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:28.140
and it seems to dislike the ocean. This area...

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:31.590
Oh! Caracal-san, Serval-san, are we ready?

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:33.430
Okay, let's go!

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:36.490
Oh, and the four gods were 
located in the same place

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:39.080
as the valuable thing I mentioned before.

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:40.260
Signing off for now!

00:07:41.650 --> 00:07:46.330
I didn't really understand all of that. 
Did something happen at this mountain before?

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:51.780
The Cerulean from before!

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:53.530
We have to go rescue them!

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:56.330
Serval-chan, we should go 
to the mountain peak first.

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:56.840
Huh?

00:07:56.840 --> 00:08:01.040
The things Mirai-san said... 
They might have been about that Cerulean.

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:11.590
Wow... So this is what it's like up here!

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:16.510
That's Sandstar. But what's the other stuff?

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:22.850
If what Mirai-san said is correct, 
then those "four gods" things should be here.

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:26.270
Serval-chan, let's look for 
anything that stands out.

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:26.860
Huh?

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:28.730
Something's here.

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:31.570
I have this feeling that we should find
it now, while we have the chance.

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:32.860
Got it!

00:08:35.980 --> 00:08:37.700
D-Don't eat m—

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:40.970
Order: Carnivora
Family: Procyonidae
Genus: Procyon

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:40.970
I finally caught you, you hat thief, you!

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:42.510
Huh? Hat?

00:08:42.510 --> 00:08:43.490
H-Huh?

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:49.340
Got it!

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:52.340
What are you doing? She wouldn't steal!

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:56.340
You lie! She wants to have 
the treasure all to herself.

00:08:57.900 --> 00:09:00.030
At long last, I got it back!

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:01.820
I'll just put this here, and...

00:09:01.820 --> 00:09:03.340
Kaban-chan, are you okay?

00:09:03.340 --> 00:09:06.370
Y-Yeah. Startled, but okay.

00:09:06.370 --> 00:09:09.230
Huh? Is Kaban-san nearby?!

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:13.440
She's Kaban-chan. Who are <i>you</i>?

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:14.870
H-Hello...

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:18.410
What? There's no way <i>you</i> could be Kaban-san!

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:34.720
Order: Carnivora
Family: Canidae
Genus: Vulpes

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:22.590
No, she's Kaban-chan! 
Wait, are there more Kaban-chans?

00:09:22.590 --> 00:09:25.270
Kaban-san is heroic.

00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:28.010
She makes bridges, ends wars...

00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:30.370
She even knows PPP!

00:09:30.370 --> 00:09:33.100
I'm telling you, that was Kaban-chan.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:37.390
Raccoon-san, looks like you did it again.

00:09:37.390 --> 00:09:38.430
Huh?

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:40.460
She's Kaban-san.

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:44.310
I knew she was showing up in an awful lot 
of the same places as the hat girl...

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:50.400
B-But I found this first. 
She stole it from me!

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:53.920
Do you think Kaban-san would steal, though?

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:58.570
You've been singing her praises. You even 
said you owe your life to her, didn't you?

00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:00.930
I'm sure there must be an explanation.

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:07.320
Here... I'll give it back, for now...

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:09.050
Thank you.

00:10:09.050 --> 00:10:13.040
I'm sorry for jumping on you.

00:10:16.330 --> 00:10:19.180
There it is! This is what I wanted to hear!

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:23.430
You mean Mirai-san's messages? 
Let's listen together, then.

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:27.560
The locations: east, west, south, 
and north from the crater center.

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:33.440
According to the pamphlet, 
the crossing at 3-E is dead center.

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:36.110
This statue is of the Eastern Azure Dragon,

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:39.150
so I believe there will be three more buried.

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:43.940
If it's really filtering the Sandstar Raw here,

00:10:43.940 --> 00:10:47.200
you could say that to this island, 
it's a true treasure.

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:48.830
Let's see...

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:54.510
"3-E" would be... where this and this connect?

00:10:54.510 --> 00:10:57.090
I wonder what "east, west, 
south, and north" means...

00:10:57.090 --> 00:11:01.180
The sun rises in the east 
and sinks in the west, so...

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:03.760
I bet this arrow means north.

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:05.260
Fennec?!

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:07.990
Since Raccoon-san's always running off,

00:11:07.990 --> 00:11:11.110
I have to know how to navigate 
with the stars and sun.

00:11:11.110 --> 00:11:13.480
That's incredible, Fennec-san.

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:15.960
I knew you were amazing, Fennec.

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:18.610
I have no idea what you're talking about.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:23.490
That means... here and here... 
and there'll be something here, too...

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:25.490
Found one!

00:11:25.490 --> 00:11:26.710
Me, too.

00:11:26.710 --> 00:11:29.580
I can't find one over here!

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:31.480
One's missing?

00:11:31.480 --> 00:11:35.400
Could that have something to 
do with this thin substance?

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:42.110
What is it, Kaban-chan?

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:46.260
No, it's nothing. Let's search Raccoon-san's area.

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:50.700
What the?

00:11:51.490 --> 00:11:53.960
What's it doing? What ability is that?

00:11:56.070 --> 00:11:59.400
A bluff? We'll finish you off right now!

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:03.130
What's happening?

00:12:03.130 --> 00:12:04.030
This...

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:06.550
Don't tell me it's...

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:09.290
What in the world is that?

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:22.010
Not good. We have to strike <i>now</i>!

00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:27.180
It's not stopping.

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:29.720
What do we do, Brown Bear-san?

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:31.810
You get Monkey out of here! I'll...

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:43.760
Kaban-san! We found it!

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:45.160
I'll dig it out.

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:48.160
Got it! Once it's out, move it over here.

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:51.620
Large volume of Sandstar Raw discharged.

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:54.460
Appearance of Colossal-class 
Cerulean expected.

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:58.460
Due to a park emergency, 
visitors are to evacuate immediately.

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:02.010
The nearest evacuation route
is Sunrise Harbor.

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:05.920
Due to a park emergency, 
visitors are to evacuate immediately.

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:06.640
Lucky-san... This isn't the time for...

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:11.760
No. Ensuring the safety of park visitors 
is my job as a park guide robot.

00:13:11.760 --> 00:13:13.310
Please evacuate immediately.

00:13:13.310 --> 00:13:15.200
The nearest evacuation route—

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:16.440
Lucky-san.

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:18.920
I'm not a visitor.

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:22.980
The others have helped me so, so much.

00:13:22.980 --> 00:13:28.180
If something's happening to the park, 
I want to do whatever I can for them.

00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:40.460
Understood, Kaban. If it becomes 
too dangerous, be sure to run.

00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:44.600
Setting Kaban as a temporary park guide. 
Guide permissions allowed.

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:46.200
Here it is!

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:47.520
What do we do with it?

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:50.010
What is it, Boss? Let's hurry along.

00:13:54.770 --> 00:13:57.640
What's wrong? Is it in the wrong place?

00:13:57.640 --> 00:13:59.570
Kaban. The height.

00:13:59.570 --> 00:14:00.900
Oh, right!

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:14.880
Is that all we need to do?

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:17.540
Yeah. I think that'll do it.

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:21.820
It stopped?

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:25.090
It did stop, but it's still...

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:35.630
We're safe...

00:14:35.630 --> 00:14:39.020
Not yet, we aren't. It'll find other 
victims if we don't do something.

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:43.520
R-Right... But how can 
we defeat that big thing?

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:46.190
Brown Bear! Monkey!

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:47.690
Are you okay?

00:14:49.380 --> 00:14:50.820
This is the plan.

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:53.500
As of now, the black Cerulean is in this area.

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:55.860
We'll be luring it over to the ocean.

00:14:55.860 --> 00:15:01.000
I believe that it's heading toward 
the sun because it follows lights.

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:05.410
So we'll wait until after the sun's 
down and use the bus to lead it.

00:15:05.410 --> 00:15:07.720
If the Cerulean loses sight of the vehicle,

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:10.630
or if there are any other problems, 
we'll lead it with fire.

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:12.470
What's "fire"?

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:14.160
Oh, um...

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:16.180
This.

00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:21.040
Oh, right. None of you 
want to hold fire, do you?

00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:22.100
Really?

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:23.900
Brown Bear-san, are you okay with it?

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:26.780
Sure. It doesn't scare me that much.

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:29.530
Then I'll be counting on you to handle it.

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:32.470
Once we're near the ocean, 
all of you should run away.

00:15:32.470 --> 00:15:36.200
You're not going to go into the ocean yourself, 
right? Do you have another way?

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:40.370
I'll use light to lure it to the boat, 
and then sink it once it's on board.

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:44.000
That's Kaban-san for you. So wise!

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:45.390
Huh? The boat?

00:15:45.390 --> 00:15:46.630
You can't, Kaban-chan!

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:49.390
Don't you need that boat so 
you can search for humans?

00:15:49.390 --> 00:15:53.680
It's okay, Serval-chan. The safety of everyone
and the park matters more right now.

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:58.280
If we manage to lure the Cerulean there, 
Lucky-san and I will operate the boat.

00:15:58.280 --> 00:16:02.850
Raccoon-san and Fennec-san, I need you 
to guide any Friends away from the area.

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:03.870
Gotcha.

00:16:03.870 --> 00:16:05.310
Understood!

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:07.720
I can't say if it will work, but...

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:11.360
No. We'll make it work.

00:16:11.360 --> 00:16:14.370
I'm sorry. You were supposed 
to use that boat...

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:17.370
No. I only just learned about it, anyway.

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:18.530
I'm ashamed.

00:16:18.530 --> 00:16:21.790
None of you are Hunters, and now 
you're caught up in the danger...

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:26.620
Hey, don't say that. When the park needs 
saving, we all have to save it together.

00:16:26.620 --> 00:16:30.500
You've been fighting for us all along 
behind the scenes, haven't you? Thanks.

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:35.130
Kaban-san said it herself: 
divide difficulties up among the group.

00:16:35.130 --> 00:16:38.050
Huh? Did I say that?

00:16:38.050 --> 00:16:42.840
With Kaban-san and me here, we're invincible!

00:16:42.840 --> 00:16:45.640
Oh, really? Do you have a special skill?

00:16:45.640 --> 00:16:49.160
She can run full tilt toward 
the day after tomorrow.

00:16:49.160 --> 00:16:51.180
Is that a good idea?

00:16:55.890 --> 00:16:58.200
Okay, mission start!

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:06.860
It's looking our way!

00:17:06.860 --> 00:17:07.780
Lucky-san!

00:17:07.780 --> 00:17:08.540
Understood.

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:15.490
It's following!

00:17:15.490 --> 00:17:18.680
Okay, let's get it to the harbor 
while holding this distance.

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:26.440
So far, so good.

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:36.530
I knew we could count on Boss's driving!

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:37.780
Leave it to me.

00:17:41.270 --> 00:17:42.010
Boss!

00:17:42.010 --> 00:17:43.350
Lucky-san?!

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:46.040
Ka...

00:17:47.700 --> 00:17:49.110
...boom!

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:53.210
Boss! You're so cool today!

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:56.010
Keep it up. Once we see the boat, 
all that's left will be...

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:01.690
Huh?

00:18:01.690 --> 00:18:02.720
What's it doing?

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:20.710
Kaban-chan! Boss!

00:18:26.320 --> 00:18:27.460
Serval-chan!

00:18:31.300 --> 00:18:32.290
You okay?!

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:35.310
Serval-chan... Serval-chan, she...

00:18:35.310 --> 00:18:38.030
It's too big for me to take on alone...

00:18:38.030 --> 00:18:41.840
If you get eaten, you'll die... 
Your memories will...

00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:45.400
If the bus doesn't work, 
we lead it by fire, remember?

00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:48.030
If we fail, there'll be more casualties.

00:18:48.030 --> 00:18:50.580
Or you can run and save yourself.

00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:54.130
Just know that running at it now 
would waste her sacrifice.

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:03.010
Once the Cerulean is in position
close to the boat,

00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:06.530
Lucky-san, turn on its lights and start it.

00:19:06.530 --> 00:19:10.290
Keep your distance from it. 
It might change shape again.

00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:13.420
I'll carry Boss. Can you run?

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:14.080
Yes.

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:18.920
Without the bus, we only have this torch.

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:22.560
This plan will only work at night. 
We have to hurry.

00:19:22.560 --> 00:19:24.430
We'll sink it for sure.

00:19:28.430 --> 00:19:29.460
Let's move!

00:19:30.850 --> 00:19:33.560
For the time being, we have to get 
far enough that it can't catch up...

00:19:34.740 --> 00:19:36.110
Where is she?!

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:03.590
This distance should do it...

00:20:29.560 --> 00:20:30.410
Meow...

00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:33.920
Meow... meow!

00:20:34.240 --> 00:20:39.050
Meow, meow, meow, meow!

00:20:42.340 --> 00:20:45.550
Hang on, Serval-chan. I'm coming for you!

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:16.180
Serval-chan!

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:25.300
Serval-chan. Serval-chan!

00:21:28.580 --> 00:21:31.110
Wake up, Serval-chan. We need to run!

00:21:42.640 --> 00:21:43.900
Serval-chan.

00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:46.860
I look useless at a glance.

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:51.860
I didn't even know why I was born. 
But you accepted me.

00:21:53.100 --> 00:21:54.830
You've looked out for me all this time.

00:22:13.880 --> 00:22:14.930
Thank you.

00:22:16.040 --> 00:22:16.990
Be well.

00:23:52.850 --> 00:23:54.670
Next time: "Amusement Park."
